cinnamon-clipboard (1.3.4) noble; urgency=medium

  Added:
  * Ignored applications: copies made in listed applications (password
    managers by default) are never recorded.
  * Pause button in the quick menu and the main window.
  * The welcome wizard asks whether to check for updates at startup.

  Changed:
  * Build the Debian package from debian/ with dpkg-buildpackage.
  * New maintainer: Akos Keresztes; update checks point to xsak/cinnamon-clipboard.
  * History mode is a single Persistent | Temporary switch in Preferences.
  * "Clear history" moved to Preferences and asks for confirmation.
  * The quick menu shows more items, scaled to the screen height.
  * Share a single .desktop file between the launcher and autostart.
  * Remove RPM packaging; Linux Mint is the supported target.

  Fixed:
  * Paste on select only pastes into the window that was active when the
    quick menu opened.
  * Switching from temporary to persistent history no longer deletes it.
  * The quick menu keeps the first item selected when the search field
    gets the focus.
  * Make the history database, images and configuration private to the user,
    and always overwrite deleted items in the database file.
  * Avoid freezes and dropped paste requests when copying files.
  * Complete translations for all new text.

 -- Akos Keresztes <akos.keresztes@gmail.com>  Tue, 03 Nov 2026 22:13:07 +0100

cinnamon-clipboard (1.3.4~beta6) noble; urgency=medium

  Added:
  * Pause button and a "recording is paused" notice with a Resume button
    in the main window.

  Changed:
  * Move "Clear history" to Preferences and ask for confirmation first
    (Cancel is the default).

  Fixed:
  * Saving Preferences no longer undoes a pause made in another window.

